course: dictionary
lesson: 13796
title: Inversion: turning things the other way round
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inversion means turning something upside down or the other way round. Picture a cup turned over so the water spills out. The cup is still there, but its position has flipped. «She turned the bowl upside down to dry it» is an inversion of the bowl.
explain: The same idea works with words. In «You are ready», the subject «you» comes first. In «Are you ready?», the verb «are» moves in front of «you». Grammar calls this changing the usual order of words. A clue: many questions start with a helper verb like «Are», «Do» or «Can».
explain: Maths uses inversion too. Addition and subtraction undo each other: if you add 5 and then subtract 5, you end up where you started. When you divide by a fraction, you flip the fraction and multiply instead. Reverse, flip and undo all point to the opposite direction.
explain: Weather can invert as well. On some cold, still mornings, warm air sits on top of cold air near the ground. This is a temperature inversion, and it traps fog and smoke so the air feels thick and dirty. When a word seems to mean its opposite, check the sentence for clues like «reverse», «flip» or «undo».
fact: Inversion means turning something upside down or the other way round.
fact: «The roller coaster loop gave the riders an inversion, turning them upside down.»
fact: In grammar, «Are you coming?» uses inversion: the verb comes before the subject.
fact: In maths, inverse operations undo each other, such as addition and subtraction.
fact: A temperature inversion is warm air sitting over cold air near the ground, which can trap fog and smoke.
exercise: Inversion means turning something upside down or the other way round. Which picture fits? | A cup being washed | A cup filled to the brim | *A cup turned upside down | A cup with a lid on
exercise: In «Are you coming to the park?», what has been inverted? | *«Are» moves before «you» | «The» is missing | «Coming» moves before «park» | Nothing has changed
exercise: Maths: inverse operations undo each other. What is the answer to 12 + 7 − 7? | *12 | 0 | 19 | 5
test: In «Do you like maths?», the helper verb «Do» comes first. What is this called? | Rhyme | Synonym | *Inversion | Addition
test: On a cold, still morning, fog hangs low over the town because warm air sits on top of cold air. What is this called? | Word order | *Temperature inversion | Roller coaster loop | Fraction
exam: What does inversion mean in maths? | *Reversing or undoing, such as flipping a fraction | Rounding to the nearest ten | Adding more numbers together | Drawing a perfect circle
